            text: "One good pad is the minimum for low, flat-landing problems. Two pads is the realistic answer for most outdoor bouldering, because falls travel and a single pad rarely covers the whole landing zone. Three or more pads, usually pooled across a group, become necessary for highballs, traverses, and boulders with sloping or rocky bases.",
